B = [
    ('Rolls-Royce', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Rolls-Royce, monumental, upright and hushed grandeur. Tall, formal, near-vertical fronts crowned by a tiny winged figurine, long smooth rolling proportions, flat slab sides and one thin chrome line along the flank. Mirror-polished bright metal with slim fluted vertical slats, deep lustrous paint in claret, silver sand, midnight blue or black, often in two tones with a lower band of silver. Interiors are hand-stitched cream or tan leather, deep wool pile, burr walnut veneer with fine inlay and organ-stop metal pulls. Tall narrow wheels with plain polished centres and a small double-R mark. Dignified, imposing, effortless and quiet.'),
    ('Bentley', 'Europe', '1920s-30s and 1950s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Bentley, muscular, wide and heavy British grand touring. A broad mesh grille in a chrome surround topped by a small winged B mark, powerful haunches, a long bonnet, a deep sculpted shoulder line and a low planted stance on large wheels. Early forms are open, riveted and raw in dark racing green with leather straps and wire spokes, later forms are polished chrome, diamond-quilted leather in contrasting hides, knurled metal switchgear and open-pore burr wood. Colours are deep green, dark blue, silver, black and burgundy. Powerful, hand-finished, gentlemanly and substantial.'),
    ('Jaguar', 'Europe', '1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Jaguar in the 1960s, long, low, sensuous and feline. A very long sweeping bonnet, a tight cabin set far back, an oval open-mouth front, headlamps faired smoothly under glass, flowing curved wings and a tapering fastback tail on slim pillars. Delicate chrome, wire-spoke wheels with centre spinners and a leaping cat motif at the nose. Paint in British racing green, signal red, cream, metallic silver-blue and opalescent grey. Interiors in red or tan leather, polished wood, rows of toggle switches and big chrome-ringed white-faced dials. Elegant speed, curvaceous and graceful.'),
    ('Aston Martin', 'Europe', '1960s and 2000s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Aston Martin, lean, refined and quietly aggressive British grand touring. A long bonnet, short rear overhang, a wide trapezoid mouth of horizontal slats in a bright surround, side gill vents behind the front wheels, a low rakish roofline falling to a clipped tail and a muscular flowing haunch. Slim swept lamps and a crisp rising shoulder line. Winged marks at nose and tail. Colours of silver birch, racing green, midnight blue and gunmetal. Hand-stitched quilted leather, contrast piping, polished glass controls, fine wood or carbon weave. Sleek, taut, understated and elegant.'),
    ('Mini', 'Europe', '1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Mini in the 1960s, tiny, boxy, cheeky and playful. A two-box shape with a wheel pushed to every corner, very short overhangs, flat upright ends, a roof like a small lid and tiny wheels. Round chrome lamps, thin chrome frames, external welded seams, exposed hinges and slim bumpers. Bright paint in tartan red, island blue, white and racing green with a contrasting white roof and bonnet stripes. Interiors are bare and minimal, with one central round gauge pod, rubber mats, ribbed vinyl and a row of toggle switches. Compact, friendly, honest and fun.'),
    ('Land Rover', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Land Rover, rugged, honest and farmyard-tough utility. Flat slab aluminium panels, an upright bluff front with a plain rectangular grille and round lamps set into the wings, a square bonnet with exposed hinges, squared wheel arches, a boxy cab and a short stubby stance on chunky treaded tyres. Safari-style roof racks, canvas tops and a spare wheel carried on the outside. Matt olive green, bronze green, sand, poppy red and pale grey with white roofs. Spartan interiors of painted metal, bare rubber mats, simple dials and tough fabric. Utilitarian, hard-working and unpretentious.'),
    ('Lotus', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Lotus, extremely low, light, stripped and track-bred. A thin fibreglass shell, a sharp wedge or rounded teardrop nose, a roofline barely above knee height, wide haunches over small wheels, bare minimal bumpers and a high tapering tail. Small round or pop-up lamps, small finely spoked or cast star wheels and a round green and yellow badge. Colours of racing green with a bright yellow stripe, bright yellow, white, orange and metallic silver. Interiors are basic and cramped with thin bucket seats, exposed aluminium and small instruments. Minimal, purposeful, nimble and lightweight.'),
    ('Morgan', 'Europe', '1930s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Morgan, hand-built, charming and deliberately pre-war. A long louvred bonnet, separate sweeping cycle-type wings, a narrow flat cockpit, a rounded tail and a tall upright chrome front with a slim vertical bar. Freestanding round lamps on stalks, spare wheel on the rear, wire spokes with knock-off hubs, aluminium panels over ash wood, folding canvas hoods and leather straps. Racing green, claret, cream, navy and ivory with polished brass and chrome. Leather seats, polished wooden dash, round white-faced dials and thin wooden wheel. Handcrafted, nostalgic and cheerful.'),
    ('Austin', 'Europe', '1930s-50s', 'cars', 'In the style of Austin in the 1930s to 1950s, rounded, upright, sensible and homely British family motoring. A tall chrome upright grille, curved separate wings, running boards on early forms, large round lamps on the wings, side-louvred bonnet, rounded boot and narrow bumpers with small guards. Thin steel wheels with chrome caps and a small winged mark. Paint in black, maroon, deep green, grey and cream, often two-tone. Interiors in beige or maroon leather, polished wood dash with one small central dial, large thin-rimmed wheel and thick carpet. Stately, modest, dependable and comfortable.'),
    ('Triumph', 'Europe', '1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Triumph sports cars in the 1960s, breezy, sporty and affordable open two-seaters. A long low bonnet, a tidy tapering tail, chrome bumpers, rounded sculpted wings with a crisp crease, lamps tucked into a smooth nose, a small mesh grille with a round shield mark and a folding black cloth hood. Wire-spoke or steel wheels with chrome trim rings. Signal red, white, British racing green, pale yellow and deep blue. Interiors with black or red vinyl bucket seats, wood or painted dash, round dials, toggle switches and a wood-rim wheel. Jaunty, compact and cheerful.'),
    ('MG', 'Europe', '1930s and 1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of MG, small, jaunty British open sports motoring. A tall upright chrome radiator of vertical slats under an octagon badge, a long flat louvred bonnet, cutaway doors, cycle wings, a rounded tail with a spare wheel and a low folding windscreen. Later forms are smooth with chrome bumpers and wire spokes. Racing green, red, cream, ivory and pale blue. Bucket seats in red or black leather, engine-turned or wooden dash with chrome-rimmed dials and a slim banjo-spoke wheel. Spirited, cheerful, plucky and simple.'),
    ('Volkswagen', 'Europe', '1950s-60s', 'cars', 'In the style of Volkswagen in the 1950s and 1960s, cute, honest, friendly and economical. One smooth continuous beetle-like curve with a domed roof, rounded bonnet, bug-eye lamps standing up on the wings, no grille, tiny oval windows, slim chrome bumpers and sweeping fenders. Small steel wheels with chrome caps and a round badge. Pastel beige, sea blue, coral red, mint green, ivory and cream. Interiors are bare painted metal with a single round dial, thin two-spoke wheel, plain cloth or vinyl and exposed painted door panels. Simple, rounded, practical and charming.'),
    ('Porsche', 'Europe', '1960s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Porsche, compact, balanced, purposeful and athletic. A smooth teardrop profile with a sloping fastback roofline falling from the windscreen to the tail, round lamps rising from flared front wings, a low rounded nose, wide muscular rear haunches, short overhangs and a small spoiler. Modern forms add a thin full-width light bar at the tail. Five-spoke or star-pattern forged wheels. Guards red, silver grey, signal orange, racing yellow, pale blue and black. A crest badge with a rearing horse. Interiors with five round dials in a row under a deep hood, black leather, houndstooth cloth and aluminium trim.'),
    ('BMW', 'Europe', '1970s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of BMW in the 1970s and 1980s, precise, driver-focused and understated sporty design. A crisp three-box shape, thin pillars, a large glasshouse, a low nose with a twin grille of two slim vertical oval openings with chrome bars, paired round lamps, a sharp shoulder line from nose to tail and a short boot with a slight forward-leaning shark stance. Cross-spoke wheels with a blue and white roundel. Silver, bright blue, henna red, black, white and fjord grey. Interiors with a driver-angled dash, black cloth or leather, clear round dials and plain brushed trim.'),
    ('Mercedes-Benz', 'Europe', '1960s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Mercedes-Benz in the 1960s to 1980s, upright, dignified, solid and formal engineering. A tall chrome grille crowned by a three-pointed star on the bonnet, wide chrome surround, vertical lamps, flat sides with sharp creases, thin pillars with a large glasshouse, chunky bumpers with rubber strips and ribbed tail lamps. Steel wheels with chrome caps. Champagne, ivory, signal red, midnight blue, silver grey and black. Interiors with wide tufted velour or leather, walnut trim, large rotary controls and a big four-spoke wheel with a padded centre. Substantial, formal, safe and meticulous.'),
    ('Audi', 'Europe', '1980s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Audi, clean, precise, taut and technical. A large single-frame hexagonal grille with horizontal bars in a bright or black surround, four interlocking rings at the nose, sharp tight surfaces, a taut shoulder line, flush glass, crisp LED lamps with a distinct light signature, a slim roofline and a wide light bar at the tail. Multi-arm alloy wheels. Glacier white, grey, black, tango red and navy. Interiors with a flat machined look, aluminium trim, perfect panel gaps, round vents, black or grey leather, a flat-bottom wheel and digital displays. Crisp, engineered and understated.'),
    ('Opel', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Opel in the 1960s and 1970s, neat, compact, sporty and stylish mass-market design. A wide low nose, a rectangular black-mesh grille with a lightning bolt mark, a coke-bottle waist rising toward the tail, small chrome bumpers, thin pillars, a gently curved fastback and flared arches. Round or rectangular lamps, neat rectangular tail clusters, steel wheels with chrome caps. Signal yellow, bright orange, lime green, white and sky blue. Interiors with bucket seats in checked cloth or vinyl, a simple dash with round dials and a thin wheel. Tidy, youthful and sporty.'),
    ('Citroen', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Citroen in the 1950s to 1970s, futuristic, quirky, avant-garde and comfortable. A low streamlined teardrop body that seems to crouch, a sloping shark nose, a tail that tapers narrowly, smooth skirts covering the rear wheels, a minimal slot grille, a double chevron mark and lamps behind smooth glass. A single-spoke steering wheel and thin pillars. Pale green, ivory, grey blue and sand beige, or bold orange and brown, with white roofs. Interiors with a very low bench seat, checked cloth, pod-shaped instruments and odd plastic controls.'),
    ('Peugeot', 'Europe', '1980s-2000s', 'cars', 'In the style of Peugeot in the 1980s and 1990s, neat, compact, well-proportioned and sporty. A clean wedge profile, a small rampant lion mark on the nose, a rectangular black grille between slim wraparound lamps, smooth uncluttered flanks with one crisp line along the doors, black plastic bumpers, tidy rectangular tail lamps and a rising beltline. Neat alloys with five or six holes. White, bright red, ocean blue, silver, dark green and black. Interiors with deep-pile cloth, a simple dash with a round binnacle of clear dials, grey plastic and thin stalks. Tidy, practical and lively.'),
    ('Renault', 'Europe', '1970s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Renault in the 1970s and 1980s, cheerful, functional, boxy and French-practical. A square nose, flat bonnet, huge flat rectangular lamps, a large diamond mark centred on a flat black grille, an upright windscreen, large squared glass, flat side panels with plastic rub strips and fat black bumpers. Steel wheels with small plastic caps. Bright orange, yellow, vivid red, light blue, off-white and beige metallic. Interiors with bold striped or checked cloth, a flat black or brown dash, a round instrument binnacle and big stalks. Compact, sunny and unfussy.'),
    ('Bugatti', 'Europe', '1930s', 'cars', 'In the style of Bugatti in the 1930s, sensuous, artistic, elegant and aristocratic coachbuilt sculpture. A tall horseshoe-shaped nickel-polished front dominating the nose with a small red oval mark, a long bonnet with fine louvres, flowing swept wings, a boat-tail or teardrop rear and a steeply raked windscreen. Eight-spoke cast alloy wheels and large round lamps. French racing blue, black over red, deep cream and two-tone schemes with a polished metal spine. Interiors with soft red or brown leather, engine-turned aluminium dash, small round dials and a thin wood wheel.'),
    ('Delahaye', 'Europe', '1930s', 'cars', 'In the style of Delahaye in the 1930s, flamboyant, theatrical, curvaceous Art Deco coachwork. Very long sweeping lines, a teardrop body, pontoon wings flowing over the wheels, a long bonnet running into a sloping tail, a narrow upright grille with fine chrome bars, tapering lamps faired into the wings and chrome spears running through the wing. Pierced disc or wire wheels with chrome caps. Two-tone schemes such as ivory over dark blue, silver over burgundy and deep black. Interiors with cream or red leather, an engine-turned dash with round dials and a delicate wheel.'),
    ('Alfa Romeo', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Alfa Romeo in the 1960s and 1970s, passionate, lively and graceful Italian sports design. A low slim body with a distinctive triangular shield at the nose flanked by mesh, a circular badge with a red cross and crowned serpent, rounded lamps under glass or set in the wings, a long bonnet, small cabin, pointed tapered tail and truncated rear. Chrome bumpers, thin pillars and five-hole alloys. Alfa red, white, light blue, silver and dark green. Interiors with bucket seats, a large wooden wheel with drilled aluminium spokes and deep-set round dials.'),
    ('Ferrari', 'Europe', '1960s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Ferrari in the 1960s to 1980s, sensual, dramatic and fast. A low, wide body with a long curved bonnet or wedge nose, round or pop-up lamps, an egg-crate mesh front, large air intakes, curvy haunches, a fastback roof with flying buttresses or side strakes and a rounded tail with four round lamps. A prancing black horse on a yellow shield. Wire spokes or five-star alloys with a centre nut. Rosso red, giallo yellow, silver, black and dark blue. Interiors with tan or black leather, an exposed metal gear gate, a deep-dish wheel and rows of round dials.'),
    ('Lamborghini', 'Europe', '1970s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Lamborghini in the 1970s and 1980s, brash, theatrical and futuristic. An extremely low flat wedge with a pointed nose, razor-sharp creases, pop-up lamps and a body barely waist-high. Hexagonal intakes, louvres along the rear deck, scissor-style doors rising up, flat black louvred panels and wide rear wheels with huge tyres. A golden bull on a black shield. Cast star or telephone-dial wheels. Vivid lime green, orange, yellow, white, red and purple. Interiors with angular black leather, a wedge dash with small switches and pod dials and a small wheel. Extreme, dramatic and showy.'),
    ('Maserati', 'Europe', '1960s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Maserati, graceful, smooth, refined and elegant Italian grand touring. A long bonnet, tight fastback roofline, a large oval grille with vertical chrome bars bearing a trident mark, curvy muscular wings, three small port-shaped vents in the front wing, slim lamps, boomerang-shaped rear lights and wide sculpted haunches. Polished multi-spoke or wire wheels. Deep blue, silver, dark burgundy, pearl white and black. Luxurious tan, red or cream leather with fine stitching, polished wood or carbon trim and an analogue clock at the centre of the dash.'),
    ('Lancia', 'Europe', '1950s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Lancia in the 1950s to 1980s, refined, finely detailed, understated and intellectual with a gentle sporty edge. A narrow shield-shaped chrome grille, a small flag mark bearing a lance, slim lamps, tidy proportions, delicate pillars, a large glasshouse, thin chrome trim along the flanks and a slightly tapered tail. Rally forms have boxy flared arches, white or grey roofs and wide blue and red stripes. Pale grey, midnight blue, cream, ivory and rich burgundy. Interiors with wool or velour, wood veneer, neat round dials and a wide thin wheel.'),
    ('Fiat', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Fiat in the 1950s to 1970s, tiny, round, cheerful and playful post-war Italian city design. A bulbous egg-shaped body, a short nose, tiny bug-like lamps, a flat or lightly curved roof sometimes rolled open as canvas, thin chrome bumpers, a small badge and a simple tail with a small window. Small steel wheels with chrome caps. Pastel yellow, powder blue, light green, cream, cherry red and white. Interiors with a bare metal dash painted body colour, a single round speedometer, thin-rimmed wheel and simple vinyl or fabric seats.'),
    ('Volvo', 'Europe', '1960s-90s', 'cars', 'In the style of Volvo in the 1960s to 1990s, boxy, upright, sturdy, safe and rational Swedish design. A flat bonnet, a large diagonal strip across the grille bearing a circle with arrow mark, square lamps, a boxy glasshouse with upright pillars, a flat-sided body with a thin crease, big square tail lamps, black bumpers with rubber trim and a long flat roofline. Plain steel or simple five-hole alloy wheels. Beige, forest green, mustard, silver, white and dark blue. Interiors with thick supportive seats in plaid cloth or leather, a flat dash with large clear dials and a big wheel.'),
    ('Saab', 'Europe', '1970s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Saab in the 1970s and 1980s, aeronautical, quirky, practical and eccentric Swedish design. A short stubby nose sloping down, a deeply curved windscreen, a rounded cockpit-like cabin, a wide hatch tail, rectangular lamps with tiny wipers, a small grille with a gryphon head on a red circle, black plastic bumpers and a distinctive curved roof pillar. Alloys with a distinct hole pattern. Black, silver metallic, deep red, white and dark blue. Interiors with deep bucket seats in grey or blue cloth, an asymmetrical wraparound dash with big round dials and floor-mounted controls.'),
    ('Tatra', 'Europe', '1930s-40s', 'cars', 'In the style of Tatra in the 1930s and 1940s, streamlined, futuristic, odd and aerodynamic. A long smooth teardrop body, a central stabilising fin running down the rear deck, a tapering tail with cooling louvres, a bulbous nose with a third lamp at its centre, smooth flush sides, curved windows, a split rear window and skirted wings. Steel disc wheels with chrome caps. Dark green, black, metallic grey and burgundy. Interiors with wide bench seats in cloth or leather, a wooden dash with simple dials and a slim large wheel.'),
    ('Skoda', 'Europe', '1960s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Skoda in the 1960s to 1980s, small, plain, boxy, honest and rugged Czech design. A flat bonnet, round lamps, a simple small grille, chrome-rimmed bumpers, a smooth unfussy body, slim roofline, large flat windows and a sloping rear with a louvred cover. A winged arrow mark on the nose. Steel disc wheels with tiny caps. Pale beige, olive green, sky blue, mustard yellow and brick red. Interiors with plain vinyl, a flat plastic dash in grey or brown with a strip speedometer and a big thin wheel. Modest, utilitarian and unpretentious.'),
    ('Trabant', 'Europe', '1960s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Trabant in the 1960s to 1980s, tiny, boxy, austere, humble and slightly smoky East German design. A flat bonnet, pressed plastic body panels, flat sides, square corners with slight rounding, round lamps, a small slim grille, small chrome bumpers, a short upright tail with a tiny rear window and thin pillars. Tiny wheels on steel rims with plain caps and a small letter T mark. Pastel pale blue, beige, sage green, orange and white with a faded matt finish. Interiors with a bare flat dash, a single round speedometer, thin-rimmed wheel and plain hard vinyl.'),
    ('Seat', 'Europe', '1970s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Seat in the 1970s and 1980s, compact, square-cut, sunny, simple and affordable Spanish design. A flat bonnet, a plain rectangular grille, square lamps, black plastic bumpers, crisp straight body lines, a flat roof, an upright rear window, boxy glass and flat doors. A small stylised S mark on the nose and tidy rectangular tail lamps. Steel wheels with small caps or simple alloys. Bright red, yellow, white, silver and dark blue. Interiors with striped cloth seats, a flat dash with simple round dials and a small wheel.'),
    ('Alpine', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Alpine in the 1960s and 1970s, tiny, rounded, low, nimble, light and rallying French design. A fibreglass body with a swooping curved roofline, a short nose with round lamps set in the front, smooth rounded wings, a small oval air intake, a very low windscreen and a rear window sloping into a short tail. Small wide steel or alloy wheels with chrome nuts. Bright blue, orange, white and yellow, often with stripes along the bonnet. Interiors with cloth and vinyl bucket seats, a simple dash with round dials and a small leather wheel.'),
    ('Koenigsegg', 'Europe', '2000s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Koenigsegg, hyper-sleek, exotic, clean and ultra-technical Swedish engineering. A low wide body, a smooth rounded nose with a thin split splitter, narrow slit lamps, a bubble canopy cabin, doors that swing up and out, a rounded rear with a carbon wing and exposed bare carbon fibre weave under clear lacquer. Hollow carbon or forged five-spoke wheels. Ice blue, gloss white, orange and gunmetal. A ghost-like shield mark. Minimal interiors of carbon, leather and aluminium with a small vertical display and a small wheel.'),
    ('Spyker', 'Europe', '2000s', 'cars', 'In the style of Spyker in the 2000s, bold, eccentric, ornate Dutch hand-built luxury that mixes aircraft cues with opulence. A nose shaped like a round propeller hub with a circular grille of spoke-like bars, a bulging body with exposed round lamps, a compact cabin, wide flared rear wings, a round exhaust and a spare wheel emblem. Polished multi-spoke turbine-like wheels. Bright orange, lime green, black, silver and pearl white. Interiors with diamond-quilted leather in contrasting colours, exposed turned aluminium, big round white-faced dials, a drilled wheel and a cockpit feel.'),
    ('Simca', 'Europe', '1950s-60s', 'cars', 'In the style of Simca in the 1950s and 1960s, jaunty, post-war and optimistic French pontoon design. A rounded body, small tail fins, a wide-mouth chrome grille, round lamps, a wraparound windscreen, chrome trim strips along the flanks, a rounded tail with chrome bumpers, a swallow mark on the nose and pastel two-tone paint. Steel wheels with chrome caps and whitewall tyres. Cream over sea green, pink over grey, turquoise and sand. Interiors with bench seats in vinyl and cloth, a painted dash with chrome-ringed dials and a large white wheel.'),
    ('Hispano-Suiza', 'Europe', '1920s-30s', 'cars', 'In the style of Hispano-Suiza in the 1920s and 1930s, aristocratic, grand and sculptural luxury touring. A long louvred bonnet, a tall narrow radiator, a stork in flight on the cap, large freestanding round lamps, flowing separate wings, running boards and coachbuilt bodies in polished wood or aluminium. Wire spokes or large steel discs. Deep blue, burgundy, black and silver with polished brass or nickel brightwork. Interiors with deep buttoned leather, polished burr walnut and fine instruments in round brass or chrome bezels.'),
    ('Bristol', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Bristol in the 1950s to 1970s, discreet, reserved, hand-built and clubby British grand touring with an aircraft-inspired shape. A long bonnet, a small oval nose with twin kidney-shaped openings, round lamps set in the wings, a smooth aerodynamic body, a gently curved roof, hidden details behind flaps and a subtle sculpted tail. Steel wheels with simple chrome caps. Dark green, grey, cream, black and claret. Interiors with deep leather, polished walnut, clear round dials and a thin large wheel.'),
    ('Facel Vega', 'Europe', '1950s-60s', 'cars', 'In the style of Facel Vega in the 1950s and 1960s, rich, glamorous and jet-age French grand touring. A long bonnet, a wide egg-crate grille set low in the nose, stacked lamps in vertical pairs, a wraparound glass windscreen with thin pillars, large chrome bumpers, tail fins, a flat boot and chrome side strips. Wire spokes with knock-off hubs. Black, silver, bright red, cream and deep blue. Interiors with leather, a dash filled with white-faced dials and toggle switches in polished metal and a wide-rim wooden wheel.'),
    ('Pagani', 'Europe', '2000s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Pagani in the 2000s to present, jewel-like, rounded and artisan handcrafted Italian hypercar design. A rounded organic body, a short nose with oval lamps blending into the wings, a bubble-shaped cabin, four exhausts stacked in the centre of the rear, round tail lamps, a tall carbon wing, exposed carbon weave and fine polished aluminium details. Forged turbine-like wheels with five bolts. Deep blue, silver, black and tricolour stripes. Interiors with milled aluminium controls, exposed carbon, tan leather in fine stitching, a round gear gate and many tiny details.'),
    ('DS', 'Europe', '1950s-60s', 'cars', 'In the style of DS in the 1950s and 1960s, futuristic, serene and floating, like a spaceship. A long sloping shark nose, a streamlined body that tapers narrowly at the rear, a floating white fibreglass roof, a very low front with a simple slit grille, lamps behind glass, smooth skirts over the rear wheels, thin pillars and a chevron mark. Steel disc wheels with small caps. Pale grey, ivory, sea green, pastel blue and sand. Interiors with a one-spoke wheel, plush cloth or leather and a dashboard shaped in smooth curves.'),
    ('Ford', 'North America', '1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Ford in the 1960s, honest, approachable, everyday mass-market American design. A long hood, short rear deck, wide low stance, a flat horizontal grille with a small galloping horse or oval blue badge at its centre, triple vertical tail lamps in chrome bezels, a sharp scalloped crease along the side and a chrome strip along the flank. Plain steel wheels with chrome caps or five-slot styled wheels with whitewall or red-line tyres. Vinyl bench seats, painted metal dash with round gauges and woodgrain trim. White, poppy red, turquoise, pale yellow and dark green with moderate chrome.'),
    ('Chevrolet', 'North America', '1950s', 'cars', 'In the style of Chevrolet in the 1950s, cheerful, optimistic diner-era American design. A wide egg-crate grille, bright chrome bumpers with round bullet guards, a low hood, twin chrome rocket ornaments, a gold bowtie badge, sharp tail fins with chrome trim, a sweeping two-tone side spear, a wraparound windshield and a thin-pillar hardtop roofline. Whitewall tyres and full chrome hubcaps. Interiors of two-tone vinyl with chrome-ringed gauges and a big thin wheel. Turquoise and ivory, coral and white.'),
    ('Cadillac', 'North America', '1959', 'cars', 'In the style of Cadillac in the late 1950s, excessive, glamorous, jet-age opulence of vast length and width. Towering pointed tail fins with twin bullet tail lamps, heavy chrome bumpers with large conical guards, a jewelled egg-crate grille, dual stacked lamps, a long flat hood, a thin hardtop roof, stainless trim and a wreath and crest mark. Pink, pearl white, powder blue and black paint with chrome everywhere. Interiors of tufted leather, thick carpets and sparkling dash trim.'),
    ('Buick', 'North America', '1950s', 'cars', 'In the style of Buick in the 1950s, comfortable middle-class luxury, rounded and heavily chromed, dignified rather than flashy. A toothy chrome grille like a wide smile, large round chrome bumper guards, a row of three or four round portholes on each front fender, a sweeping chrome side spear that dips along the doors, a slightly bulbous body, curved glass and whitewall tyres. Chrome-covered wheels with a tri-shield mark. Plush two-tone fabric and a wide chrome dash with a big round speedometer. Cream, sea green, coral and maroon.'),
    ('Pontiac', 'North America', '1960s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Pontiac in the 1960s and 70s, aggressive, swaggering street-racer American muscle. A split twin-nostril grille divided by a body-coloured beak, stacked or hidden lamps, a long hood with a raised scoop, a coke-bottle waistline swelling over the rear wheels, tall haunches, a trunk spoiler, bold stripes and a red arrowhead mark. Brushed metal rally wheels with bright trim rings, black vinyl bucket seats and an engine-turned dash with round gauges. Carousel red, deep green, ivory and bright orange, plus a large bird decal on a black hood.'),
    ('Dodge', 'North America', '1970s', 'cars', 'In the style of Dodge in the early 1970s, brutal, loud, cartoonish tough-guy American muscle. A wide aggressive stance, a long flat hood with twin bulging scoops, a split grille with hidden or twin round lamps, squared-off fenders with a pronounced coke-bottle hip, a bold bumblebee stripe or tail band and a ducktail spoiler. Steel wheels with slotted rims and fat white-letter tyres, a pistol-grip shifter and black vinyl bucket seats. High-impact violet, lime green, purple, bright orange and pale green, with a ram or red stripe mark.'),
    ('Chrysler', 'North America', '1957-1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Chrysler, late 1950s and early 60s forward-look American design, space-age, optimistic and airy. Very low and wide with tall swept-back tail fins, a long slender profile, a huge expanse of glass in a wraparound windshield, a wide-mouth grille with a bright bar, canted dual lamps in chrome pods and flowing side chrome with a contrasting colour panel. A pentastar or winged mark, big round tail lamps and radial-spoke wheel covers. Push-button controls on the dash, sculpted panels and luxurious fabric. Turquoise, flamingo pink, cream and charcoal.'),
    ('Lincoln', 'North America', '1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Lincoln in the 1960s, understated, sober, expensive American flagship luxury. A slab-sided perfectly flat body, a thin knife-edge beltline, a restrained bright grille of fine horizontal bars, rear-hinged doors, a long level hood, a square formal roofline, a star mark in a plain rectangle, minimal chrome in a thin shoulder strip and slim vertical tail lamps. Plain wheel covers. Inside, a flat dash with brushed metal and deep leather with a feeling of grave dignity. Black, midnight blue, silver and white.'),
    ('Jeep', 'North America', '1940s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Jeep, rugged, utilitarian, honest, military-derived adventure design. A flat boxy body, a seven-slot upright grille flanked by round lamps, exposed hinges and bolts, a flat folding windshield, squared-off wheel arches, short overhangs, removable doors, soft canvas or hard tops, a spare tyre on the tailgate and heavy black plastic fender flares. Painted steel bumpers, tall knobby tyres on steel or black wheels and red tow hooks. Hose-down interiors with grab handles and bare painted metal. Olive drab, sand, desert tan, safety yellow and bright orange.'),
    ('Tesla', 'North America', '2010s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Tesla, minimalist, clean, futuristic and software-first electric design. Smooth unbroken body surfaces, a closed-off nose with no grille, a low sloping fastback roofline, flush door handles, slim LED lamps, a thin horizontal tail light bar, a large glass roof, frameless windows and a plain T-shaped mark. Aerodynamic turbine-style wheels with flat covers, body-coloured trim and almost no chrome. A stark white or black cabin with a single huge landscape touchscreen, a matte wood or plain strip and no buttons. Pearl white, solid black, deep blue metallic, midnight silver and red.'),
    ('Studebaker', 'North America', '1950s', 'cars', 'In the style of Studebaker in the 1950s, quirky, futuristic and a bit strange American design. A pointed bullet nose like an aircraft spinner at the centre of the grille, a low wide stance, a thin wraparound rear window, a slim body with a long low hood, a low roofline, an almost European flat-sided silhouette and a gently tapering tail. Chrome bumpers, small fins and round tail lamps. Gold or turquoise hardtops. Pale pastel two-tone paint in pink and white, sky blue and cream. A streamlined dash with a big round dial and brushed metal.'),
    ('Packard', 'North America', '1930s-40s', 'cars', 'In the style of Packard in the 1930s and 40s, stately, hushed, old-money American luxury. A tall narrow ox-yoke grille shaped like a pointed shield with fine vertical bars, a very long hood, sweeping separate fenders, chrome-ringed lamps on the fender tops, a chrome flying mascot on the radiator, running boards, a long wheelbase and a formal upright cabin. Wire or disc wheels with whitewall tyres. Deep gloss black, maroon, dark green and cream with a thin coach line. Walnut veneer, mohair or leather and elegant engine-turned metal.'),
    ('Hudson', 'North America', '1948-1954', 'cars', 'In the style of Hudson in the late 1940s and early 1950s, hunkered, bathtub-shaped and solid American design. A step-down body with a very low floor, a bulbous slab-sided shape with rounded fenders, a wide low simple chrome grille with a triangle mark, a smooth slab trunk, a fastback roofline, skirted rear wheels, small windows, a heavy brow over the lamps and a rounded tail. Two-tone paint in maroon and cream, deep green and tan. Chrome caps with whitewalls and a thin chrome strip along the flank. Deep seats, a big wheel and a plain dash.'),
    ('Oldsmobile', 'North America', '1950s-60s', 'cars', 'In the style of Oldsmobile in the 1950s and early 60s, jet-age, confident and glossy American rocket-themed design. A bright wide grille with a central round intake like a jet engine, a chrome rocket-ship ornament on the hood, a sweeping chrome spear down each flank, a wraparound windshield, a hardtop roof with thin pillars, small tail fins and bullet-shaped tail lamps. Chrome wheel covers with spinner centres. Two-tone vinyl and gleaming dash trim with a ribbon speedometer. Rocket red, white, mint green and sky blue.'),
    ('DeSoto', 'North America', '1950s', 'cars', 'In the style of DeSoto in the mid to late 1950s, dramatic and theatrical American design. A tall vertical oval grille like a pursed mouth, a huge chrome bumper wrapping around the nose, heavy chrome brows over twin lamps, tall pointed tail fins with arrow-shaped trim and a long sweeping side chrome spear splitting the two-tone paint. A hooded roof, a wraparound screen, wide whitewall tyres and full-disc hubcaps. A bold dash, push-button shifter and plush fabric. Pink and charcoal, turquoise and white, sunset orange.'),
    ('Edsel', 'North America', '1958-1960', 'cars', 'In the style of Edsel in 1958, overwrought, odd and unforgettable American design. A tall vertical horse-collar grille set in the middle of a wide bumper, a pointed hood crease and a split nose, wingtip boomerang tail lamps, gull-wing chevrons at the rear, side sculpting with a bright spear and a cut-away dip along the door. Pillarless hardtops with a smooth cabin. Wheels with chrome rims and whitewalls. A rolling-dome speedometer and push buttons on the steering hub. Two-tone pink and black, turquoise and white, yellow and brown.'),
    ('Tucker', 'North America', '1948', 'cars', 'In the style of Tucker in 1948, futuristic and streamlined rear-engined American design. A very low, smooth, rounded fastback body like a teardrop, three lamps with the centre lamp in the nose turning with the steering, a narrow chrome-bar grille with a wide mouth, a swept-back roof, a fully enclosed louvred rear, broad rear fenders and slim tail lamps. Chrome bumpers, a thin trim line, small whitewall tyres and plain caps. A padded dash, central gauge cluster and bench seats. Waltz blue, beige, maroon and dark green.'),
    ('DeLorean', 'North America', '1980s', 'cars', 'In the style of DeLorean in the 1980s, matte, metallic, sci-fi, raw and unfinished. A flat angular wedge body of bare brushed stainless steel panels with visible grain and no paint, a low long nose, razor-sharp creases, upward-opening gull-wing doors, a flat louvred rear window cover, black plastic bumpers and a rear engine grille. Slim flat lamps in a plain black nose strip, a rectangular rear lamp bar and five-spoke dished wheels in dark grey. Grey leather with a simple flat dash and rectangular gauge pods.'),
    ('Plymouth', 'North America', '1957-1970', 'cars', 'In the style of Plymouth, bold and cheeky American design from 1957 through the 1960s. Sharp tall tail fins that blade backward, a flat wide bright grille with a sailing-ship mark, long sculpted flanks with a sweeping two-tone chrome sweep, dual lamps, a very low hood, a full-width chrome bumper and a large thin roof with a huge rear window. Muscle forms add a bold hood scoop, a tall rear spoiler and loud decals with a cartoon bird. Chrome-rimmed wheels with whitewalls. Purple, vivid orange, lemon yellow and bright green.'),
    ('Mercury', 'North America', '1949-1950s', 'cars', 'In the style of Mercury in the late 1940s and 1950s, low, mean and smooth custom-friendly American design. A smooth rounded slab body, an optional low chopped roofline, a heavy chrome horizontal bar grille with a big central ornament, fat round bumper guards, teardrop fender lines flowing into the doors, a shortened hood, a sloped fastback, small tail lamps in a rounded rear and a chrome strip along the flank. Skirted rear wheels, whitewalls and chrome flipper hubcaps. Candy maroon, primer grey, gloss black and cream. A bench seat and a long dash band.'),
]
